From 5daa287c386b982009ac3b8ab88cbf5ae6941497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ingo Franzki <ifranzki@linux.ibm.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:01:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c: Fix X25519 EVP_PKEY_METHOD derive on
 s390x

The X25519 EVP_PKEY_METHOD function s390x_pkey_ecx_derive25519() passed
the private and public key to s390x_x25519_mul() in swapped order,
so it returned X25519(clamp(peer_pub), own_priv).  When that output
reached the peer, one output recovered the private key with one scalar
inversion.  Restore the proper argument order.

This only affected the legacy code path, the provider code path
was not affected.  The legacy code path is only used when an engine
is registered or an application method was added.

Fixes: 3cca05cc194c "s390x: fix ecx derive"
Reported-by: Bhabani Sankar Das <007bsd@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Ingo Franzki <ifranzki@linux.ibm.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Bob Beck <beck@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Nov  6 19:42:43 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33556
---
 crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c b/crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c
index bc5cb0ed147d..1f3442f772f9 100644
--- a/crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c
+++ b/crypto/ec/ecx_meth.c
@@ -1198,7 +1198,7 @@ static int s390x_pkey_ecx_derive25519(EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx, unsigned char *key,
 
     if (!validate_ecx_derive(ctx, key, keylen, &privkey, &pubkey)
         || (key != NULL
-            && s390x_x25519_mul(key, privkey, pubkey) == 0))
+            && s390x_x25519_mul(key, pubkey, privkey) == 0))
         return 0;
     *keylen = X25519_KEYLEN;
     return 1;
